# dsec sandbox environment — docker/.env template.
#
# Copy to docker/.env (git-ignored) and fill in DEEPSEEK_API_KEY:
#   cp docker/.env.dsec.example docker/.env
#
# Then:  ./run-dsec.sh up        (full stack with the DeepSeek sandbox)
#        ./run-dsec.sh doctor    (boot diagnosis, no API cost)
#
# Only the DeepSeek-specific values are listed here; every other setting
# keeps the docker/.env.example default. See docs/dsec-sandbox.md.

# ── dsec: DeepSeek sandbox environment ──────────────────────────────
# Selects the DeepSeek Harness environment (dsh --profile headless) as the
# coding agent for the worker. "deepseek-harness" selects the same adapter
# under its canonical name; "dsec" is the environment alias.
UC_CODING_AGENT=dsec

# Required. dsh authenticates from the environment; get a key at
# https://platform.deepseek.com
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# Optional. Point dsh at a proxy/gateway instead of the public DeepSeek API
# (e.g. an OpenAI-compatible gateway that fronts DeepSeek models).
# DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=

# Optional. Custom dsh config/credentials directory (defaults to ~/.dsh).
# The sandbox env allowlist does NOT forward DSH_HOME to agent subprocesses
# (deny-by-default); to use a custom directory add it explicitly:
#   UC_SANDBOX_ENV_EXTRA=DSH_HOME
# DSH_HOME=
